1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:08,295
Welcome to North America episode one of three. First, I clear the chosen names
for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:08,974 --> 00:00:18,308
We begin with the two countries that fill the north and the middle of the
continent: Canada above, and the United States below it.

3
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:22,390
Let's bring Canada and its neighbours into view.

4
00:00:25,218 --> 00:00:44,154
Canada occupies the northern half of the continent, from the Pacific coast to
the Atlantic and Arctic Ocean. Its only land border is with the United States,
along the 49th parallel, and its islands continue far north of the mainland.

5
00:00:44,818 --> 00:01:04,222
Its name comes from kanata, "village" in an Iroquoian language, which Jacques
Cartier recorded in 1535 and which was later applied to the whole land. It has
the longest coastline of any country in the world, and by one count it holds
more lakes than all the rest of the world together.

6
00:01:04,886 --> 00:01:15,033
Picture Canada as the great northern shield: an enormous coastline and an
enormous number of lakes, with the United States along its southern edge.

7
00:01:15,704 --> 00:01:19,245
Let's bring United States and its neighbours into view.

8
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:38,041
The United States spans the middle of the continent, with Canada along its
northern border and Mexico along its southern one. Alaska reaches far to the
northwest across the Pacific, and Hawaii lies beyond the mainland in the
Pacific.

9
00:01:38,695 --> 00:01:58,927
America comes from Amerigo Vespucci, the Florentine navigator whose name a
German mapmaker put on the New World in 1507. Yellowstone, set aside in 1872,
was the first national park in the world, and Alaska and Hawaii joined as
states only in 1959.

10
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:12,377
Hold the United States as the middle band of the continent: one country
touching Canada above and Mexico below, with two far-flung states added in the
same year, 1959.

11
00:02:15,921 --> 00:02:31,149
Canada lies north of the United States and shares its only land border with
it. Canada is the northern shield with the longest coastline in the world; the
United States is the middle band between Canada and Mexico.

12
00:02:31,801 --> 00:02:45,361
Remember a village name that became a whole country, and more lakes than the
rest of the world, in the north. Remember Vespucci, Yellowstone and two states
added in 1959, in the middle.
